course: dictionary
lesson: 15910
title: Unnecessary: not needed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unnecessary means not needed. If you could do without something and nothing would go wrong, it is unnecessary. «It is unnecessary to bring an umbrella, because the sky is clear and blue.» You can leave the umbrella at home, and nothing goes wrong.
explain: Unnecessary can also mean more than is needed or fair. «The teacher gave unnecessary homework on top of the work we already had.» Too much homework is more than is needed, so it is unnecessary. Ask yourself: if I took this part away, would the answer still work? If yes, it was unnecessary.
explain: Maths problems often hold unnecessary information. «Sam has 5 red pens and 3 blue pens. How many pens does he have?» The colours do not change the count, so you can ignore them. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "The extra part is not needed to answer the question" still makes sense.
fact: Unnecessary means not needed, so you could do without it.
fact: The opposite of unnecessary is necessary, which means needed.
fact: «Unnecessarily» is the adverb: «She shouted unnecessarily» means she shouted for no good reason.
fact: In maths, unnecessary information is extra detail you can ignore.
fact: «Unnecessary risk» means a danger you did not need to take.
exercise: «The sign was unnecessary, because everyone already knew the way.» What does unnecessary mean here? | *Not needed | Made of wood | Written in red | Very large
exercise: Ali has 4 apples and 2 bananas. He also has a blue bag. Which part is unnecessary information for counting the fruit? | The 2 bananas | *The blue bag | The 4 apples
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unnecessary? | *Necessary | Careless | Simple
test: «Dad said the trip to the shop was unnecessary, because we had plenty of food.» What does unnecessary mean? | Very fun | Long and tiring | *Not needed | Paid for in advance
test: «She shouted unnecessarily at her little brother.» What does unnecessarily mean? | In the right way | Very quietly | With a big smile | *For no good reason
exam: Which is an unnecessary risk? | *Climbing on a wet roof just for fun | Wearing a helmet when cycling | Looking both ways before crossing the road | Holding an adult's hand near the road
